# Base URL of the NestJS backend API this frontend calls.
# Read server-side only (the async Server Component in src/app/page.tsx), so it
# has NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and is never inlined into the browser bundle.
# Never expose secrets via NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars; real secrets live in the team
# secret manager and, for Vercel, in the project's Environment Variables settings.
#
# This value is for local development only. Do NOT set it on Vercel: the root
# vercel.json declares a service binding that makes Vercel generate and inject
# BACKEND_URL itself, pointing at the backend service in the same deployment.
# Setting it by hand there would only override a value that is already correct,
# and correct per deployment, so a preview reaches its own backend rather than
# production's.
#
# Bindings resolve at runtime, not during the build. That suits this app, because
# the home page renders on demand, but it means build-time code cannot read it.
# See "Deploying to Vercel" in the root README.md.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
